A||||10||Philphine||khumo victoracers||||1||
Z||000000||Philphine||11-10-2001||01:59 AM||||<BR>well, i guess that was a mistake. i got them off ebay because i wanted to try the size (245/45-16). just got home to look at them. the guy had said he used them one weekend but they look pretty worn out. then i looked at the treadwear rating. 50? maybe it's true. i knew it was a popular autox tire but i guess thats really about all it is. <P>not sure what i'll do with 'em. maybe put them on anyway and get a feel for the size like i intended.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||thomas_l||11-10-2001||07:43 AM||||How much did you pay? I think those are around $130 new from Tirerack. They will look worn when they are brand new - there's only 6/32" of tread before they get shaved and/or heat cycled. They are competition tires and definitely consumables  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||11-10-2001||08:23 AM||||$110 shipping included. not the biggest loss, but i probaly wouldn't have got them knowing what i know now. i may keep them till spring and try them or see if i really want to try autox and keep them for that. <P>how long do you think they'd last as street tires? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||11-10-2001||11:25 AM||||You can get about 9 months  out of them street driving. My dad has them on his 911 , there a great tire. A little suseptible to grooves in the road though. <P>They really don't start to work to full potential until about the 4th event their used at. When they look worn out with barely any tread left showing is when their at their best. Another local 911 owner drove his car everyday in the summer with them on and autocrossed it on weekends. He got a whole summer out of them<P>Fact is they don't last too long , and being an autocrosser compound they can reach a point where the tire gets too hot and the rubber gets squirmy (slang for the tires go away) I don't reccomend them for a track event , but we loved using them on the street. They won't overheat unless you really push them hard<P>A better all around street tire is a Bridgestone SO3. Friend of mine runs them on a Mr2 and there a very competitive street tire.<P>All depends on what you use the car for.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sleeper||11-10-2001||11:32 AM||||yea, what Slammed said. you'll get about 10 thousand miles out of them.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||11-10-2001||11:43 AM||||ok. except for the coming season i can live with that. maybe i'll stick 'em on anyway and work a little harder at replacing my truck for real winter weather.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Eric||11-10-2001||12:38 PM||||I barely get 10,000 miles out of my 36k miles tires!  Usually I multiply the TWR by 10 then divide by 2.  That gives me a good idea of how long the tires are going to last on a properly aligned car driven kind of hard.  For me, I take that figure and divide by 2 again.||||reg||1
Z||000007||lowCG||11-10-2001||06:23 PM||||Those will be SO much fun,you'll probably get addicted!||||reg||1
Z||000008||kempo||11-10-2001||07:50 PM||||I recently got Kuhmo Ecsta's on my 17" wheels for the Fiero.  Worst tire purchase I've had to date.  These tires handle horribly and I would consider them utter crap.  Thank God for a 30 day satisfaction garuantee!  Think I'll be getting those Michelin's I've been eyeing over...<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/gtsmall.jpg">    <BR>0-60 6.9 seconds||||reg||4
Z||000009||Slammed Fiero||11-10-2001||07:58 PM||||Kuhmo Ecsta's are meant to satisy the "Big Tire for little money" market<P>The 911 weighs about 150lbs less than a Fiero , but it's weight characteristics are about the same though. The tires stand up well and I think aroun 7500 miles would be a good guesstimate as to how long they would last.<P>Michelin's MMX sport tires are what we run on the 911 onthe street wheels , good tires , but no where near the Kuhomo's , or a good set of Pirelli's. Michelin used to make a different compund sport tire , but has since discontinued it. It was a softer tire than the regular sports. Much more suited as a dual purpose tire.<P>I was really impressed with the bridgestone S03 pole position's. But with the amount I drive the car Toyo RA1's are lookin mighty nice too (we have them on the vair)<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Master_Sushi||11-10-2001||08:48 PM||||I had a 16inch set of *Kumho* ECSTA Supra 712's on my old fiero. These were great tires! I don't know someone could say they were crap. I had my coupe up to top speed a few times (well over 110), and they were completely smooth. Handeling was GREAT on them. They wore pretty well also, I only had them on for a summer though.<P>You can read the reviews on them, almost all of them are very good.||||reg||1
